# Git guesses text-vs-binary by looking for a NUL byte in the first 8000
# bytes, and some PDF writers put their entire header and cross-reference
# table in plain ASCII — so a perfectly ordinary PDF can read as text. The CI
# whitespace scan is `git grep -I`, which honours this attribute and nothing
# else: without the line below it walks into a PDF's xref table, finds the
# trailing spaces the format requires there, and fails the build.
#
# It also keeps `git diff` from dumping these files into the terminal.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
